Subject: [PATCH] Phase 12 done
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unknown-command reply: change from hardcoded '2#' to firmware-matching '0' (no '#').

Firmware analysis (ProcessCmds.cpp poll()):
  numericReply initialised true before dispatch. Unknown command paths:
  Case A — no handler claimed the command: numericReply stays true → '0'.
  Case B — handler claimed prefix, CE_CMD_UNKNOWN, never cleared numericReply:
           numericReply still true → '0'.
  Case C — handler set *numericReply=false before CE_CMD_UNKNOWN:
           poll() skips numericReply block; reply='' → strlen=0 → nothing written.

Root change in CommandFramer.cpp:
  dispatchFrame() now initialises numericReply=true (matching firmware's poll()).
  !handled || error==CE_CMD_UNKNOWN: write '0' if numericReply=true, nothing if false.
  This makes all three cases correct without any handler-level convention change.

Handler changes (14 files):
  All handlers that produce '#'-terminated text replies or suppress-frame
  no-reply responses now explicitly set *numericReply=false, which is required
  because the dispatcher init changed from false to true. Numeric-reply paths
  already set *numericReply=true (or use replyNumericOk/Fail) and are unchanged.
  ParkHandler and TelescopeHandler had their (void)numericReply casts updated
  to explicit assignments or comments. FaultInjector error tests updated from
  '2#' to '0' to match the corrected wire format.

New tests (test_command_framer.cpp):
  UnknownCommandReturnsZeroNoHash — Case A: '0' no '#'.
  HandlerSetsUnknownNumericReplyTrueProducesZero — Case B: handler claims prefix,
    CE_CMD_UNKNOWN, numericReply untouched → '0'.
  HandlerSetsUnknownAfterNumericFalseProducesNothing — Case C: handler sets
    *numericReply=false then CE_CMD_UNKNOWN → nothing written.
